Poker Squares SysOp Docs.
-------------------------

   Poker Squares is Visual Solitaire card game that takes place in a 5x5 grid.
This game has been designed to work on almost any AmigaBBS because it is a
STDIO AmigaDos Door.

To Install:

First make sure that you have a directory called PokerSquares/ in DOORS:  The
game itself doesn't have to be in there but that is where the Game stores its
data file at. Once that is done copy PokerSquares to that directory or DOORS:
if you want the 68000 version of the game.  Otherwise, if you have a faster
processor rename one of the PokerSquares.0x0 files to PokerSquares and copy
it to the directory.

As for setting it up on the BBS the Doors works as following from CLI:

PokerSquares HANDLE

where PokerSquares is the program itself and HANDLE is the User's handle

For CNet it would be as follows:

Dos FileName: Doors:PokerSquares/PokerSquares
 Description: Poker Squares
   Arguments: "%1"

Disable More: YES!

So that should help you set it up for like DLG or E or something :) less you 
really really dumb.

Also the Source Code has been included in the game so you can modify it and
recompile it if you wish.  Sorry I was in a hurry with this game.  So this
isn't my best work and the code is kinda sloppy in one gigantic .c file and
a .h file.  the game should recompile in SAS with "sc PokerSquares.c link"

